<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Dar Masalit</h1><p class="st-meta">1874 CE – 1922 CE (approx.) · capital Geneina</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A sultanate of the Masalit people in western Darfur that defeated a French column in 1910 and joined Sudan by agreement in 1922.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masalit-people">Masalit</a> lived on the western fringe of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>. In the 1870s, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> fell to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zubayrs-bahr-al-ghazal">Zubayr's Bahr al-Ghazal</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khedivate-of-egypt">Khedivate of Egypt</a>, a Masalit holy man, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-abd-al-nabi">Ismail Abd al-Nabi</a>, built up authority among them, and his family founded an independent sultanate around 1874.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultans ruled a farming people from fortified centres, balancing between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mahdist-state">Mahdist State</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a> and the restored <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-dinar">Ali Dinar</a>. In 1910 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Taj al-Din defeated a French column at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dorothe">Dorothe</a>, though he died in the fighting. His successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bahr-al-din">Muhammad Bahr al-Din</a>, known as Andoka, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-geneina">Geneina</a> his capital.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> in 1916 and the Anglo-French border was fixed in 1919, the sultan accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indirect-rule">indirect rule</a>. Dar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masalit-people">Masalit</a> was formally joined to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/anglo-egyptian-sudan">Anglo-Egyptian Sudan</a> in 1922, keeping its sultan as a traditional ruler.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dar-masalit.jpg" alt="Dar Masalit" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Ermanarich · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Masalit.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1874 CE – 1922 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Geneina</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ismail Abd al-Nabi, Taj al-Din, Muhammad Bahr al-Din</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Masalit, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sudan">Sudan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sultanate of Dar Masalit, Masalit Sultanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1898&amp;focus=dar-masalit" aria-label="Dar Masalit on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5295 1677 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dar Masalit lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5615 1933L5571 1919M5615 1933L5888 1853"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5571 1919h0M5888 1853h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5615 1933h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5615 1933h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Geneina. <a href="/atlas?year=1898&amp;focus=dar-masalit">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

